[1.103,"o","ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-oci-ha-a131705 --cloud oracle --oci-region \"$OCI_REGION\" --oci-compartment \"$OCI_COMPARTMENT_OCID\" --edition pro --openvidu-pro-license \"$OPENVIDU_PRO_LICENSE\" --deployment-type ha --certificate-type selfsigned --mode auto -y\r\n"]
[2.804,"o","warning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one\r\n"]
[11.273,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[11.273,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your Oracle Cloud tenancy (region eu-madrid-1, compartment ***); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. Template: render the high availability template into .openvidu/oracle/tf-oracle-openvidu-pro-ha.tf\r\n     and its variables into .openvidu/oracle/openvidu.auto.tfvars.json (0600)\r\n  2. Machines: create the four masters and the media nodes: master-1 installs OpenVidu and the rest join it with Terraform (about 5 minutes, then OpenVidu installs)\r\n  3. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n\r\nWarning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud…\r\n   · initialize Terraform in .openvidu/oracle (downloads the provider)\r\n"]
[41.831,"o","   · apply .openvidu/oracle (this returns when Terraform is done)\r\n"]
[326.06,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so `ov stack destroy` removes it even if the wait below fails\r\n   ✓ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud\r\n\r\n▶ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu…\r\n"]
[328.192,"o","   · waiting for OpenVidu to come up (2s elapsed): the published values are not readable yet: the store holds the access of another stack (https://51.170.45.102:6443), not this stack's (https://158.179.211.233:6443): another stack shares it; waiting for this one to publish\r\n"]
[379.579,"o","   · OpenVidu is up\r\n   ✓ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu\r\n\r\n▶ Register the stack…\r\n"]
